<div class="bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100">
  <.marketing_nav current_user={@current_user} current={:docs} />

  <section class="py-12 sm:py-16">
    <.docs_layout
      current="kubernetes"
      updated="August 18, 2026"
      toc={[
        {"prepare", "Prepare the deployment"},
        {"daemonset", "The DaemonSet"},
        {"deploy", "Deploy and verify"},
        {"visibility", "What the pod spec grants"},
        {"mutating", "Letting a node action mutate"},
        {"next", "After it is connected"}
      ]}
    >
      <.docs_header current="kubernetes">
        <:dek>
          Run one runner per node with a DaemonSet. The pod spec controls what each runner can read
          or change. This example uses the official image and persistent host storage.
        </:dek>
      </.docs_header>

      <p class="mt-6 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        To read what a containerized runner can reach, see <.link
          navigate={~p"/docs/containers"}
          class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
        >Install in a container</.link>.
      </p>

      <.docs_prerequisites>
        <:item>
          <code class="text-zinc-300">kubectl</code>
          access that can create namespaces, Secrets, and DaemonSets.
        </:item>
        <:item>
          Outbound HTTPS from every node to <code class="text-zinc-300">emisar.dev:443</code>
          and <code class="text-zinc-300">registry.emisar.dev:443</code>. See
          <.link
            navigate={~p"/docs/network-requirements"}
            class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
          >Network requirements</.link>
          for the optional GitHub fallback domains.
        </:item>
      </.docs_prerequisites>

      <.docs_h2 id="prepare">Prepare the deployment</.docs_h2>
      <.docs_callout kind={:warn} title="This manifest grants node-wide access">
        <p>
          This manifest runs as root and reads node processes, networks, journals, and files.
          Remove every grant that your packs do not need.
        </p>
      </.docs_callout>
      <ol class="mt-5 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-6 text-base text-zinc-400">
        <li>
          Create a namespace named <code>emisar-system</code>. Configure its admission policy to
          allow this host-access profile.
        </li>
        <li>
          Create a <.link
            navigate={~p"/docs/runner-fleet" <> "#enrollment-keys"}
            class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
          >reusable enrollment key</.link>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Create the Secret. Enter the key at the hidden prompt.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <.docs_code phx-no-format label="shell">kubectl create namespace emisar-system
read -rsp "Enrollment key: " EMISAR_ENROLLMENT_KEY
printf '\n'
kubectl -n emisar-system create secret generic emisar-runner \
  --from-literal=enrollment-key="$EMISAR_ENROLLMENT_KEY"
unset EMISAR_ENROLLMENT_KEY</.docs_code>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Pick the image: each runner release notes its image digest. Replace
        <code>&lt;image-digest&gt;</code>
        with the 64 hex characters after <code>sha256:</code>.
      </p>

      <.docs_h2 id="daemonset">The DaemonSet</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        This spec lets the runner observe each node. The node name is the runner identity, and
        the runner token, dispatch state, and local journal stay on the node.
      </p>
      <.docs_code phx-no-format label="yaml"><span class="text-sky-300">apiVersion</span>: apps/v1
<span class="text-sky-300">kind</span>: DaemonSet
<span class="text-sky-300">metadata</span>:
  <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: emisar-runner
  <span class="text-sky-300">namespace</span>: emisar-system
<span class="text-sky-300">spec</span>:
  <span class="text-sky-300">selector</span>:
    <span class="text-sky-300">matchLabels</span>:
      <span class="text-sky-300">app</span>: emisar-runner
  <span class="text-sky-300">template</span>:
    <span class="text-sky-300">metadata</span>:
      <span class="text-sky-300">labels</span>:
        <span class="text-sky-300">app</span>: emisar-runner
    <span class="text-sky-300">spec</span>:
      <span class="text-sky-300">hostPID</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">true</span>      <span class="text-zinc-600"># see every process on the node</span>
      <span class="text-sky-300">hostNetwork</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">true</span>  <span class="text-zinc-600"># see the node's real interfaces and ports</span>
      <span class="text-sky-300">containers</span>:
        - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: runner
          <span class="text-sky-300">image</span>: ghcr.io/andrewdryga/emisar-runner@sha256:&lt;image-digest&gt;
          <span class="text-sky-300">securityContext</span>:
            <span class="text-sky-300">runAsUser</span>: <span class="text-brand-300">0</span>  <span class="text-zinc-600"># journald + /host reads are root-only; see below</span>
          <span class="text-sky-300">env</span>:
            - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: EMISAR_GROUP
              <span class="text-sky-300">value</span>: <span class="text-brand-300">"k8s-nodes"</span>  <span class="text-zinc-600"># actions can target the whole group — one per fleet</span>
            - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: EMISAR_RUNNER_ID
              <span class="text-sky-300">valueFrom</span>:
                <span class="text-sky-300">fieldRef</span>:
                  <span class="text-sky-300">fieldPath</span>: spec.nodeName  <span class="text-zinc-600"># the node, not the pod, is the identity</span>
            - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: EMISAR_ENROLLMENT_KEY
              <span class="text-sky-300">valueFrom</span>:
                <span class="text-sky-300">secretKeyRef</span>:
                  <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: emisar-runner
                  <span class="text-sky-300">key</span>: enrollment-key
          <span class="text-sky-300">volumeMounts</span>:
            - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: state
              <span class="text-sky-300">mountPath</span>: /var/lib/emisar
            - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: audit-journal
              <span class="text-sky-300">mountPath</span>: /var/log/emisar
            - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: host-root      <span class="text-zinc-600"># node filesystem, read-only, for file inspection</span>
              <span class="text-sky-300">mountPath</span>: /host
              <span class="text-sky-300">readOnly</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">true</span>
            - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: journal        <span class="text-zinc-600"># journald logs on systemd nodes</span>
              <span class="text-sky-300">mountPath</span>: /var/log/journal
              <span class="text-sky-300">readOnly</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">true</span>
            - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: systemd-run    <span class="text-zinc-600"># systemd state, for unit status reads</span>
              <span class="text-sky-300">mountPath</span>: /run/systemd
              <span class="text-sky-300">readOnly</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">true</span>
      <span class="text-sky-300">volumes</span>:
        - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: state
          <span class="text-sky-300">hostPath</span>:
            <span class="text-sky-300">path</span>: /var/lib/emisar
            <span class="text-sky-300">type</span>: DirectoryOrCreate
        - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: audit-journal
          <span class="text-sky-300">hostPath</span>:
            <span class="text-sky-300">path</span>: /var/log/emisar
            <span class="text-sky-300">type</span>: DirectoryOrCreate
        - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: host-root
          <span class="text-sky-300">hostPath</span>:
            <span class="text-sky-300">path</span>: /
        - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: journal
          <span class="text-sky-300">hostPath</span>:
            <span class="text-sky-300">path</span>: /var/log/journal
        - <span class="text-sky-300">name</span>: systemd-run
          <span class="text-sky-300">hostPath</span>:
            <span class="text-sky-300">path</span>: /run/systemd</.docs_code>

      <.docs_h2 id="deploy">Deploy and verify</.docs_h2>
      <ol class="mt-5 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-6 text-base text-zinc-400">
        <li>Save the manifest as <code>emisar-runner.yaml</code>.</li>
        <li>Run <code>kubectl apply -f emisar-runner.yaml</code>.</li>
        <li>
          Run <code>kubectl -n emisar-system rollout status daemonset/emisar-runner --timeout=5m</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Open <a
            href={~p"/app/runners"}
            class="font-medium text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
          >Runners</a>. Confirm each node has one online runner. Tainted control-plane nodes
          are skipped unless you add a toleration.
        </li>
        <li>Run <code>debugging.loadavg</code> on one node runner.</li>
        <li>
          Open <a
            href={~p"/app/audit"}
            class="font-medium text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
          >Audit</a>. Confirm that the event records the runner, action, operator, and reason.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <.docs_h2 id="visibility">What the pod spec grants</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        <code class="font-mono">hostPID</code>
        exposes node processes. <code class="font-mono">hostNetwork</code>
        exposes node interfaces and ports. The read-only mounts expose the journal, systemd state,
        and node files under <code>/host</code>.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        The manifest uses <code class="font-mono">runAsUser: 0</code>
        because most node files and journals require root; the image otherwise runs as user <code>65532</code>. Actions run the programs inside the image, and the official image
        carries only its documented observation tools — if a pack needs another program, <.link
          navigate={~p"/docs/containers" <> "#extending"}
          class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
        >build an extended image</.link>.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        The host mounts are read-only except for runner state and its local journal. Remove <code>runAsUser</code>, <code>hostPID</code>, <code>hostNetwork</code>, or any mount your
        packs do not need.
      </p>

      <.docs_h2 id="mutating">Letting a node action mutate</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        A node mutation needs more than the read-only profile. Restarting a unit, for example,
        needs writable systemd and D-Bus sockets — mount
        <code class="font-mono">/run/systemd</code>
        and <code class="font-mono">/run/dbus</code>
        writable. Grant exactly what the intended actions need and nothing more; the runner's user
        and polkit pattern on the
        <.link
          navigate={~p"/docs/host-install" <> "#user"}
          class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
        >
          Linux host page
        </.link>
        is the same discipline on a host.
      </p>
      <.docs_h2 id="next">After it is connected</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        <.link navigate={~p"/docs/runner-fleet"} class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300">
          Manage the runner fleet
        </.link>
        covers work after the first connection — groups, labels, pack credentials, updates,
        reconnects, and removal. To roll the DaemonSet across clusters in phases, see the <.link
          navigate={~p"/docs/production"}
          class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
        >Go to production</.link>.
      </p>
    </.docs_layout>
  </section>

  <.marketing_footer />
</div>
